          <compound>
            <id type="integer">96935</id>
            <name>3-α(S)-Strictosidine</name>
            <hmdb-id nil="true"/>
            <description>3-alpha(S)-Strictosidine, also known as strictosidine or isovincoside, belongs to the class of organic compounds known as terpene glycosides. These are prenol lipids containing a carbohydrate moiety glycosidically bound to a terpene backbone. 3-alpha(S)-Strictosidine is considered to be a practically insoluble (in water) and relatively neutral molecule. 3α(S)-strictosidine is involved in some metabolic plant pathways, such as indole alkaloid biosynthesis.</description>
